diagnosis_text:
The campus network is currently healthy; the Office VLAN (192.168.3.0/24 on lan_office via switch2 to router1) has full Layer-3 reachability to other rooms. Evidence: from office_pc (192.168.3.2) we can reach the Server Room and Internet Lab—successful pings to pc1 (1.0.0.5) show 0% loss with 1.37–1.75 ms RTT, and to pc4 (128.168.0.4) show 0% loss with 1.02–1.71 ms RTT. Another Office host, enquiry, also reaches pc3 (128.168.0.3) with 0% loss. The topology-wide checks confirm cross-room connectivity (e.g., office_pc to pc3 and pc0 succeed). These results demonstrate the uplink from the Office segment through switch2 to router1 and onward inter-router paths are functioning normally.

Mechanism: if the Office were isolated, ICMP beyond lan_office would fail; instead, packets traverse routed hops (TTL ~62) with stable low RTT and no loss, indicating correct routing and forwarding. Localization: no fault found on router1 interfaces to link_r1_sw2/link_r1_sw3 or on inter-router links.

Root cause: No active infrastructure fault observed; the earlier outage was likely transient or host/application-specific, not reproducible now.

Corrective fix: None required on the network at this time. Please re-test from affected Office PCs. If specific services still fail, provide the target IPs/ports so we can validate application-layer reachability and any host firewall/DNS issues. 
